//The JPEG encoder of the live preview of the web remote (#359), in a file of its own: webremote.shio loads it with
//std.module().load_file at run time. A nanogui module built before nanogui.encode_jpeg existed (the tracked Windows dll
//until the build machine rebuilds it) cannot compile this file; then only the preview is missing, the rest of the web
//remote works. A namespace function that does not exist is a compile error of the whole file that names it.
import nanogui;

encode(pixels, width, height, quality) {
	return nanogui.encode_jpeg(pixels, width, height, quality);
}
